  "decision_conditions": [
    "The submitted drawings inconsistently depict the proposed extension with the submitted floor plans showing the extension to be partly built on the adjoining property. Class A Prior Approval application for a larger extension can only be used to extend a single property, not two. The proposals are therefore contrary to Schedule 2 Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015.",
    "Due to its siting, design and scale, it is considered that the proposed extension would have an overbearing appearance upon the existing outlook  of neighbouring no 37 Fairmead  in terms of from the existing habitable room and within the garden.  Therefore, it is considered that the proposed development would have a significant and unacceptable adverse impact on the amenities of neighbouring properties conflicting with Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy, 2012 and Council's Residential Design Supplementary Planning Document, 2013.\r\r"
  ],
